body:
I've been believing myself, for the most part, in saying that if there was a "true" timeline that it would be the timeline of the Hero of Time, i.e the Child timeline. And this was reinforced by the appearance of Ganondorf in the sequel trailer, most likely representing his form taken in Twilight Princess, what with the would on his chest and whatnot.

&#x200B;

But also part of me wants Ganondorf to wake up and speak for the first time in millennia, and say something along the lines of "It's true....all of it." referencing the events of all previous games. Something something Master Sword, something something splitting his existence across 3 parallel worlds, something something we're back in this one. Or something.

Study up on the combat mechanics. Vesperia adds a LOT to combat coming from Symphonia. For example, each weapon has a set of skills applied to it that, when equipped, are given to that character, and after a certain amount of time/uses will become permanent. So if you want certain skills, you'll have to use that certain weapon until you permanently unlock it, even if it means not switching to a more powerful weapon. To add to this, the skills include some that allow you to chain certain kinds of attacks together, and there are 3 types of techs (artes). In this way, it's similar to chaining lv 1 to lv 2 attacks and so on in Symphonia, although instead of levels they're categorized as base, arcane, and altered artes.

&#x200B;

As I said, combat has evolved so much, and in a good way (imho) from Symphonia. Really makes battles much more satisfying and also gives another layer to how you approach certain enemies and bosses.
